# Steam Deck packages INSTALLED ON EVERY TARGET (the common minimal set).
#
# FAST-INSTALL.md C2: the root image bakes exactly this closure plus the
# runtime base. Gaming-only packages live in deck-gaming.packages and the 13
# optional pre-installs in deck-preinstalls.packages -- both stay in the
# offline mirror for the early optional delta, but neither is baked.
#
# T5-fork-plan.md §3 seam S1: this list is merged into the runtime's own
# omarchy-base.packages *before* build-iso.sh copies it to
# airootfs/usr/share/omarchy-iso/, so one edit reaches all three consumers at
# once -- the offline mirror's `pacman -Syw`, the target install's
# image package set (which reads the shipped copy), and the
# `expected-packages` denominator the install dashboard draws its progress
# bar from. Appending anywhere later desyncs them.
#
# ⚠️ NO REPO-QUALIFIED NAMES IN THIS FILE. Entries here are resolved twice
# against the OFFLINE mirror, whose pacman.conf declares exactly one repo
# ([offline], configs/pacman-offline.conf) -- once by build-iso.sh's
# resolve_expected_packages and once by pacstrap at install time. A
# `jupiter-staging/foo` entry aborts both. Repo-qualified names belong in
# deck-mirror.packages, which is only ever resolved against the online repos.
# deck-nvidia-dry-run.sh refuses the build if one appears here.
#
# 🔴 THIS FILE IS THE ONLY LIST THAT INSTALLS ANYTHING OFFLINE. The line that
# used to stand here said "anything that only needs to be *available* belongs
# in deck-mirror.packages and is installed by the omarchy-deck package (seam
# S4)". THAT WAS NEVER TRUE. `omarchy-deck` declares no such dependencies and
# nothing else read that list either, so the offline mirror carried the Neptune
# kernel, the Neptune firmware and Valve's gamescope while the installed system
# got none of them -- measured on the first hardware boot,
# docs/findings/P32-steam-never-installed.md. The corrected rule:
#
#   in deck-mirror.packages ONLY          -> downloaded, kept in the mirror,
#                                            INSTALLED BY NOBODY, and after the
#                                            install the mirror is gone. Use
#                                            this only for something whose
#                                            reader is written down.
#   in deck-mirror.packages AND HERE      -> the dual-entry pattern: the mirror
#                                            list decides WHICH BUILD is
#                                            fetched (it may repo-qualify),
#                                            this list decides THAT pacstrap
#                                            installs it, offline, on the
#                                            target. `sort -u` in build-iso.sh
#                                            collapses an identical bare pair,
#                                            and the bare-form strip handles a
#                                            qualified/bare pair.
#   in deck-fetch.packages                -> not carried at all; installed over
#                                            the network at install time by
#                                            orchestrator/deck_pkgs.py.
#
# Anything that touches the boot chain is T1/T5f's, not this file's -- with the
# one deliberate exception argued in the kernel section below.
#
# --- COMMON entries: baked into the minimal image, on every variant ---------
#
# READER: pacstrap, from the offline mirror (merged into base_pkg_lists[0] by
# deck-packages.patch seam S1, which also feeds the mirror download and the
# image package set).
#
# steamdeck-dsp: Valve audio DSP firmware, COMMON (operator decision
# 2026-08-15 -- a first boot with tinny speakers is not a degradation anyone
# can act on); `jupiter-staging/steamdeck-dsp` in deck-mirror.packages decides
# the build. `steam` stays in deck-fetch.packages (Steam Subscriber Agreement;
# online only) -- do not "finish the job" here.
#
# qt6-virtualkeyboard: SDDM greeter input on a controller-only machine
# (FAST-INSTALL.md C4: Gaming=no password login + InputMethod=
# qtvirtualkeyboard via trackpad). Without it the greeter is an unanswerable
# screen -- the P32 OSK shape. extra/, redistributable (LGPL/GPL Qt).
#
# python-evdev: target-side mapper runtime for DESKTOP MODE navigation
# (stage-input-mapper). NOT a duplicate of the deck-live.packages entry,
# which serves the LIVE ISO's installer keyboard (guard 6.7) -- both lists
# need it, for different roots.
#
# omarchy-deck: our own package (seam S4); resolved against the OFFLINE
# mirror where it exists by build time. If this line goes missing the build
# stays green and the target gets nothing -- test-omarchy-deck-package.sh
# catches exactly that.
omarchy-deck
steamdeck-dsp
qt6-virtualkeyboard
python-evdev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 RETIRED 2026-09-17 (v4.0.4 rebase): the Neptune kernel is gone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This block used to pacstrap `linux-neptune-611` as THE kernel, with
# `detect_kernel` feeding archinstall `kernels=[ "linux-neptune-611" ]`.
# Operator decision 2026-09-17 adopts upstream's generic `linux-omarchy`:
# it reaches the target via the runtime's own `install/omarchy-other.packages`
# (which lists `linux-omarchy` + headers at the v4.0.4 pin) merged with this
# file into `omarchy-base.packages`, plus archinstall `kernels=` from
# `deck-form.sh`'s retargeted `detect_kernel`. No replacement line here --
# adding one would pacstrap a SECOND kernel and hand Limine a boot order to
# choose. Recorded so the next reader does not "restore" it.
#
# 🔴 linux-firmware-neptune is DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, and must not be added
# (unchanged): Valve's package conflicts against only `linux-firmware` and
# `linux-firmware-whence` while Arch ships ten split subpackages -- pacman
# removes the two it was told about and dies in the file-conflict check.
# PACSTRAP HAS NO `-Rdd` STEP. Arch's own linux-firmware-* covers amdgpu and
# the ath11k radio.
#
# ⚠️ ESP SIZE, still unmeasured: one UKI measured 74,987,520 B on hardware.
# With linux-omarchy-only there should be exactly one -- which is itself a
# thing the next build must confirm rather than assume.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MOVED TO deck-gaming.packages (FAST-INSTALL.md C2): gamescope,
# vulkan-radeon, lib32-vulkan-radeon, mangohud, lib32-mangohud.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# These install for Gaming=yes only, offline from the mirror, via the early
# optional delta (which reads deck-gaming.packages off the live ISO) and the
# C6 desktop opt-in. They were unconditional here until the four-variant
# contract: baking them would put the Gaming stack (and the NVIDIA-provider
# question the vulkan pins exist to settle) into every desktop-only image.
# deck-mirror.packages keeps the "which build" decisions (notably
# jupiter-staging/gamescope, the ONLY build shipping
# gamescope-wayland.desktop); deck-gaming.packages decides THAT they install.
# Do not re-add them here -- a second kernel-style dual install is not the
# risk, a slower minimal image and a desktop variant carrying Gaming Mode is.
